sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-overall> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Mitchison (1980, 1981) & Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) with-the-flux auxin canalization, Sachs wound bypass regeneration, and open vs closed leaf venation loops — MorphoEval overall 92.6/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Pass 2 (v2) evaluation of `1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py` (overall weighted score: 92.8/100, up from 54.5/100 in v1). The remediated script solves the Mitchison (1980) canalization bifurcation across feedback exponents p in [0.5, 2.5] (winner flux share 0.5000 at p=1.0 vs 0.9950 at p=2.0; Pearson r = 1.0000, p = 1.48e-9) and 2D cellular lamina concentration drainage (S_vein / S_par = 0.3131 vs ref 0.3100, proving S_vein < S_parenchyma); reproduces Sachs (1981) C-shaped vascular bypass regeneration around a transverse stem incision (tortuosity 1.3800, sink flux recovery 0.9852 vs 0.0804 under NPA transport inhibition); models the Feugier et al. (2005) topological transition between open venation trees (Betti-1 = 0) and closed-areole networks (Betti-1 = 14); and segments the SHA-256-locked cleared dicot leaf venation specimen (`leaf_venation_canalization_specimen.jpg`, secondary branch angle 52.93 +- 2.53 deg vs ref 54.50 deg, N = 1843 closed areoles). Overall 92.6/100 (faithfulness 92.3, reproducibility 93.4); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 94, Morphological realism / specimen match 91, Parameter expressivity 91, Morphometric validation 93, Source and data traceability 95, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins_comparison.png: rendered output of 1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py at 8871db0, image/png, 1252549 B, 2700×1680 px, artifact_sha256 1c852e279db4322139300c4c678bf8eba07a4b621122c88057d60cc618f7aff7 (sha256 1c852e279db4322139300c4c678bf8eba07a4b621122c88057d60cc618f7aff7), spec_fingerprint b1e95723b4cbd5f2bb79b0150dbb4ab3fc046d7542c48fe2c7644bb6175993d9. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: b1e95723b4cbd5f2bb79b0150dbb4ab3fc046d7542c48fe2c7644bb6175993d9; artifact_sha256: 1c852e279db4322139300c4c678bf8eba07a4b621122c88057d60cc618f7aff7; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins_reference.json=55e0f743ada83918..., datasets/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins/leaf_venation_canalization_specimen.jpg=7f67774708f8e952..., datasets/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins/paper_citations.bib=95f1b35cf42a8ae7..., datasets/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins/scout_manifest.json=94a1d6a85fe649c5...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-auxin-canalization-leaf-veins-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Mitchison (1980) Proc. R. Soc. B 207:79-109 facilitated diffusion canalization ODEs dD_ij/dt = alpha*|phi_ij|^p + beta - gamma*D_ij proving that linear feedback (p <= 1) yields diffuse flow whereas quadratic feedback (p = 2) triggers winner-take-all symmetry breaking into 1-cell-wide vascular strands where concentration drops inside the canalized vein (S_vein < S_parenchyma) | Mitchison (1981) Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B 295:461-471 & Sachs (1981) Adv. Bot. Res. 9:151-262 polar auxin transport canalization and C-shaped vascular strand bypass regeneration around a transverse stem incision | Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) J. Theor. Biol. 236:366-375 PIN1 carrier-allocation dynamics comparing open hierarchical branching venation trees against closed-areole reticulate venation loops; reconstructed_in_script: 5-regime feedback exponent sweep p in [0.5, 2.5] and 2D cellular lamina canalization solver verifying diffuse flow at p <= 1.0 (winner flux share 0.5000) vs 1-cell-wide canalized strands at p = 2.0 (winner flux share 0.9950, Pearson r = 1.0000, p = 1.48e-9) and auxin concentration drainage inside the vein (S_vein / S_par = 0.3131 < 1.0) | Sachs (1981) 20x16 cellular epicotyl transverse stem incision wound-bypass simulator reproducing C-shaped lateral deflection (4.0 cells, tortuosity L/L0 = 1.3800, sink flux recovery 0.9852) plus NPA polar auxin transport inhibitor negative control (flux recovery 0.0804) | Feugier et al. (2005) PIN1 carrier-allocated venation topology solver verifying pairwise flux conservation (antisymmetry error < 1e-14) and topological transition from open branching trees (Betti-1 = 0 loops, branch angle 52.0 deg) to closed-areole reticulate networks (Betti-1 = 14 loops, branch angle 56.5 deg) | Automated segmentation of the cleared dicot leaf venation skeleton (`leaf_venation_canalization_specimen.jpg`, primary midrib tracking, secondary vein branching angle 52.93 +- 2.53 deg, and 1843 enclosed polygonal areoles); transfer_boundary: 2D cellular lamina canalization and graph cycle-rank topology mapped to cleared dicot leaf venation skeleton; does_not_claim: 3D mechanical leaf blade expansion coupled to viscoelastic turgor-driven epidermal remodeling." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple the 2D PIN1 carrier-allocated leaf venation solver to a growing finite-element leaf blade mesh to simulate spatiotemporal order of higher-order quaternary areole subdivision." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.926"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (MorphoEval Autonomous Loop Slot 034 Pass 2 Assessor)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0009-0007-4948-9192 ;
        foaf:homepage <https://deepmind.google> .
}

